save(54,t,ch,d,inv,'The sheet names basepoint maps (31), cancels an attempted splitting of the arcs into two halves, and chooses a standard thrice-punctured-sphere group (32). There is no manuscript page numeral; archival number 53. The repeated number (31) belongs to the cancelled block and is retained. In the first paragraph the written source groups are plural (qui sont des sources), although groupe is singular. The lower relation visibly reads tilde-sigma(tilde-sigma)=1, whereas the author adds i.e. (sigma tilde-sigma)^2=1. Under conjugation notation these are not equivalent: the former forces the involution to be trivial, while the latter says that the two involutions commute. The possible intended relation tilde-sigma(sigma)=sigma is an editorial observation only. GL replaces a struck SL quotient. No claim about an abstract modular-group presentation is independently proved.',checks=[('142-054-last-relation','targeted proof check','For conjugation, t(t)=t; t(t)=1 forces t=1. For involutions s,t, (st)^2=1 is equivalent to st=ts. Therefore the written relation and its i.e. are not equivalent under that interpretation.'),('142-054-GL-identification','carried as background without fault found','The GL quotient is transcribed as the author’s replacement of SL; no independent identification is claimed.')],doubts=[('first paragraph spelling',r'\unsure{standart|standard}','standard','low'),('lower paragraph spelling',r'\unsure{standart|standard}','standard','low'),('(31), cancelled index',r'\deleted{\unsure{i}}','unrecoverable overwritten short index','low')],hand=[('Capital calligraphic G can resemble a rounded S','Open exterior with returning inner stroke at the group argument; not assumed for every later script alphabet.','H substitutes fraktur S_3 for G_3*. Aleph-like/calligraphic forms need local checking.'),('Terminal t/d in standart','Both occurrences remain unresolved; no forced normalization.','H has standard; C’s standards alternative at the first occurrence is less supported.'),('Distinct tildes survive in tiny lower-edge formulas','Both tildes in the final relation and the tilde on the rho-action are visible.','H loses one tilde in each of these two relations.')],notation=[(r'\Pi_{0,3},\widetilde\Pi_{03}','standard group and its enlargement; comma written in the first subscript, absent in the latter','Do not normalize 03 to 0,3.'),(r'=\text{ groupe}','equality sign used for même','Expand only in abbreviation list.')],abbreviations=[('= (in prose)','même'),('i.e.','id est')])
